## Model card

- **Name:** Exo Free (exo-free)
- **Short description:** **NOT AN AI MODEL.** EXO (exo-explore/exo) is an open-source framework for distributed LLM inference across consumer devices (Mac, Linux, Windows). It splits models across devices to run larger models than fit on single hardware. The "exo-free" label appears in OpenCode usage data as a provider/framework identifier, not a model. Reddit post "Exo Free - Frontier level" refers to using EXO to run models (e.g., Llama), not a model itself.
- **Provider / access:** EXO Labs (exolabs.net), GitHub (exo-explore/exo). Software framework, not a model.
- **Release / knowledge:** EXO v1.0 released ~January 2026. "12 Days of EXO" blog series Dec 2024–Jan 2025. Not a model release.
- **IDs:** No model ID. Framework: `exo` (pip/brew/dmg), `exo-explore/exo` (GitHub).
- **Context window:** N/A (framework, not model).
- **Modalities:** N/A (framework, not model).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-27):** Free open-source software (MIT license). Runs user's own models.
- **Architecture:** Distributed inference orchestration (model partitioning, device discovery, ChatGPT-compatible API). Supports LLaMA (MLX/tinygrad), Mistral, LLaVA, Qwen, DeepSeek, etc.

### Raw benchmarks found

> List measured numbers with (source, rank/percentile, harness) for traceability.
> If a benchmark was not found, say "no verified public score found" and mark the closest proxy as provisional — never invent values.

**NO MODEL BENCHMARKS EXIST.** EXO is a framework. Benchmarks on benchmarks.exolabs.net and blog.exolabs.net measure **throughput (tok/s) of other models** (Llama 3.1 8B, 70B; Qwen3-235B; DeepSeek-v3 671B) running ON EXO, not EXO itself.

- Llama-3.1-8B on RTX 3080: 104.7 tok/s — EXO benchmarks
- Llama-3.1-8B on RTX 4070 Ti: 112.4 tok/s — EXO benchmarks
- Llama-3.1-8B on RTX 4080: 120.8 tok/s — EXO benchmarks
- DeepSeek-v3 671B on 8× Mac Minis: **qualitative demo only** — EXO blog Day 2
- No model quality benchmarks (MMLU, GPQA, coding, etc.) for "exo-free".

